{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Intrusion Detection System.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Intrusion Detection System.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"intrusion detection system intrusion detection system","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Intrusion Detection System.md","fileName":"Intrusion Detection System.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Intrusion Detection System","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-09 00:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience]] [[Layered Cyber Defense and Secure Development]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience","Layered Cyber Defense and Secure Development","Intrusion Prevention System","Security Event Monitoring","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Intrusion Detection System.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Intrusion Detection System.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"intrusion detection system intrusion detection system","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Intrusion Detection System.md","fileName":"Intrusion Detection System.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Intrusion Detection System","heading":"Intrusion Detection System","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An intrusion detection system analyzes activity to identify possible attacks, misuse, or behavior inconsistent with authorized use. It can examine firewall, server, identity, and service logs for repeated login failures, unusual traffic, or attempts to retrieve inappropriate data.\n\nDetection turns raw operational records into security alerts that people or automated systems can investigate. It reports suspicious behavior; an [[Intrusion Prevention System]] additionally acts to block or contain it.\n\nAt the network layer, an intrusion detection system searches traffic for suspicious activity and known threats and records an alert when it finds them. Its evidence can feed [[Security Event Monitoring]] so observations from the network can be correlated with host and application activity.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience","Layered Cyber Defense and Secure Development","Intrusion Prevention System","Security Event Monitoring","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Intrusion Detection System.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Intrusion Detection System.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"intrusion detection system intrusion detection system","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Intrusion Detection System.md","fileName":"Intrusion Detection System.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Intrusion Detection System","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cloudcomputing_mit.epub]]\n\n[[cybersecurity.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience","Layered Cyber Defense and Secure Development","Intrusion Prevention System","Security Event Monitoring","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}